 Interpret names across the supplied original language labels: a paraphrase, inflection or word-order change need not be an exact lexical match. Use the source names and context to establish identity; do not invent translated aliases or conflate entities across graphs. If identity remains unresolved, request clarification. An alias shared by multiple identities must be clarified even if only one has the requested relation.
